+//! reads/writes whole `Vec<u8>`s.
+//!
+//! ## Authentication
+//!
+//! By default the connection is opened from `config.url` alone, with no
+//! credentials. An entry may instead name two files, `config.user_file` and
+//! `config.password_file`, holding the NATS user and password (for example the
+//! `username` and `password` keys of a Kubernetes Secret mounted into the host
+//! pod). The config carries only the paths; the files are read when the
+//! connection is opened, so the secret values never pass through the entry
+//! config. Entries with credentials are pooled apart from entries without
+//! them, and apart from entries naming different files, so an authenticated
+//! connection is never handed to an entry that did not ask for it.
 
 use std::collections::HashMap;
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
